# Line endings: LF everywhere — in the repo AND in working trees.
#
# How this works: these attributes are consulted on every `git add` (clean:
# working tree -> index, CRLF is converted to LF before hashing/storing) and
# on every checkout (smudge: index -> working tree, LF is written as-is,
# never converted to CRLF). They override each developer's core.autocrlf
# and core.eol, so the outcome is identical on every machine.
#
# They apply to all future commits; existing history keeps whatever was
# committed then. The one-time "normalize everything" commit that introduced
# this file rewrote the affected blobs, so from it on, every checkout of
# every branch is LF. If a merge ever re-introduces CRLF, repair with:
#   git add --renormalize .

*.lua      text eol=lf
*.tex      text eol=lf
*.sty      text eol=lf
*.csv      text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.txt      text eol=lf
*.sh       text eol=lf
Makefile   text eol=lf

# Binaries: never touch a byte. The QR PDFs are hand-crafted and a
# line-ending conversion would corrupt them.
*.pdf  -text
*.jpg  -text
*.jpeg -text
*.png  -text
*.eps  -text
*.kra  -text
